---
// Static about page - fully rendered by Astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout title="About - Astro + Inertia Playground">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-8 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900">About This Playground</h1>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg text-slate-600">
      <p>
        This playground demonstrates the <strong class="text-slate-900">Astro + Inertia.js</strong> integration,
        which allows you to build hybrid applications where Astro handles static content and Inertia
        powers the dynamic, authenticated portions of your app.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Use Cases</h2>
      <ul class="ml-6 list-disc space-y-2">
        <li>
          <strong>Marketing sites with dashboards:</strong> Static landing pages, pricing, and docs
          with an authenticated admin panel or user dashboard.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Gradual migration:</strong> Move parts of a Laravel app to Astro while keeping
          the interactive core powered by Inertia.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>SEO + Interactivity:</strong> Blog and documentation in Astro for SEO,
          app features in Inertia for rich interactivity.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Architecture</h2>
      <p>
        In this setup:
      </p>
      <ul class="ml-6 list-disc space-y-2">
        <li>
          <strong>Astro</strong> owns the page shell (HTML, header, footer, navigation)
          and serves static pages like this one.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Inertia.js</strong> runs inside an "island" and handles the interactive
          application region, fetching page data from your Laravel backend.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Laravel</strong> serves as the backend, providing Inertia responses
          with page components and props.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="mt-12 rounded-lg bg-indigo-50 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-indigo-900">Ready to try it?</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-indigo-800">
          Make sure you have the Vue 3 playground's Laravel backend running on port 8000,
          then click the button below to enter the Inertia-powered app.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/app"
          class="mt-4 inline-block rounded-lg bg-indigo-600 px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-indigo-700 transition-colors"
        >
          Launch App
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
